  "exact_claim": "For an infinite-genus Riemann surface with finitely many n>=3 nonplanar ambient ends, Aut_hol(S) is finite. For every translation structure on that same underlying S, the full SO(2) affine preimage and Gamma(S) intersection SO(2) are finite. The exact infinite-order norm-preserving A=(1/5)[[3,-4],[4,3]] therefore cannot even belong to the full matrix Veech group for X={0,2/3,1}.",
  "proof_gap": null,
  "source_scope": "Explicit prescribed matrix-group negative witness X={0,2/3,1}, infinite norm-preserving G generated by (1/5)[[3,-4],[4,3]]; OWR2014Question4 and included countable all-nonplanar subcase of broader RMV2017Question0.2. No exclusion of abstract cyclic groups under other matrices, n1/n2 or finite rotations.",
  "priority": "Explicit attributed application of the complete APV2020preprint/2021journal corollary and explicit ARSVW2023 translation finiteness principle. No new general theorem/construction/classification, firstness or continued-openness assertion. Earlier literal named-question negative answer/witness not established by bounded search.",
